{"author":{"id":"85a3c31a64931f83958f26b24045fef8415ea6ff04d942d15661891c77fc0695"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794350205,"nonce":"4WLy10AoVSgbyET+P/fX/F6N64k=","title":"Depth textures cannot be compared against a reference","message":"A shadow map is a depth texture read with a comparison sampler: WGSL `textureSampleCompare` and `textureSampleCompareLevel`. russl had the types (`TextureDepth2D`, `SamplerComparison`) and no way to sample them that way, which blocked porting Blinc's mesh shader (PCF shadows) to russl.\n\nAdded `t.sample_compare(sampler, uv, reference)`, fragment shaders only, and `t.sample_compare_level(sampler, uv, reference)`, which samples level 0 and runs in any stage, with the layer between the coordinates and the reference for an array texture. Both take a comparison sampler and return the fraction of the texels the reference passes against, as `f32`. Found by porting a hand-written WGSL shader, before russl 0.3.1 is published.","files":null}]}